# Roster · probe · compose

## Domain

- **Roster slot** (1–10) holds plant identity (`plant_uuid`, stash, stock/detached/active).
- **Probe** (kit 1–2) is live assignment; `assigned_plant_id` is inventory SoT.
- Retire/delete by **slot number** (`POST /roster/slots/{n}/retire`), not probe-only — stock and detached must be deletable.

## Entity-bus vs local draft

- Wizard Next and Add must not wait on bus round-trip; local picks/drafts are SoT until flush.
- Before every step advance and commit: flush strain, nickname, sprout to helpers (`syncComposeTextToBus` + `flushEntityTextDrafts`).
- Catalog strain pick is async — never commit until picked label is on the bus.

## Probe conflict hygiene (brain)

- On assign/commit to a probe: call `release_conflicting_slot_pots(pot, keep_slot)` so only one slot claims a probe.
- On slot retire: clear probe helpers, inventory `assigned_plant_id`, and **`plant_uuid`** on the emptied slot.

## SPA refresh after roster mutations

- Serialize `/fleet/computed` fetches (promise chain); bump brain `tick` on computed update.
- Cache-bust computed GET (`?_=` timestamp).
- After delete: close probe drawer with captured `retirePot === pot` — do not read stale roster from closure.

## Verification

- Roster/probe edge matrix belongs in `brain/tests/test_roster_stress.py` + `test_plant_probe.py` — browser stress alone is not sufficient proof.

## Browser compose automation (Pi SPA)

- Catalog hits: **JS `.click()`** on `.dsc-catalog-hits button` (coordinate clicks fail silently).
- Footer Next: `.dsc-btn-primary.click()` with ~3s wait between steps.
- Stock commit: review card **Add to roster (stock)** then modal **Add to Roster stock (no probe)**.
